{
 "description": "Cross-language vectors for @enkerli/upi — Serpe's UPI notation and the readings taken over a parsed pattern. @enkerli/theory's rhythm.json holds the algorithms (Bjorklund, Barlow tables, complement, codecs); this holds the layer above them, which had no coverage beyond poly.json. Steps are bit-strings, leftmost = LSB: the first character is step 0, hex digits are little-endian, and tresillo is 10010010 = 0x94 = d73. That convention is the single thing a port into a new language silently inverts, which is why the numeric forms are here. Out of scope, deliberately: R(k,n) and mutatePattern, both of which draw from Math.random and would pin nothing; and the DOM visualisers, which are app-side by design. Regenerate with gen-upi-vectors.mjs; upi.test.js asserts this file stays reproduced.",
